      "translations": {
        "en": "He said: So they were separated, and each man from them was stood against a pillar from the pillars of the mosque, and their heads were covered with their clothes. Then he called for Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', his scribe, and said: 'Bring me a parchment and an inkwell.' And the Commander of the Faithful (peace be upon him) sat in the seat of judgment, and the people sat facing him. He said to them: 'When I exclaim Takbeer, you all exclaim.' Then he said to the people: 'Go out.' Then he called one of them and made him sit in front of him, and uncovered his face. Then he said to Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi': 'Write down his confession and whatever he says.'"
